<title>USA: Calypte plans job cuts to conserve cash.</title>
<headline>Calypte plans job cuts to conserve cash.</headline>
<dateline>ALAMEDA, Calif. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calypte Biomedical Corp Monday it has begun a cost-cutting program that will significantly reduce the size of its work force and help it conserve cash.</p>
<p>Friday, Calpte said the U.S. Food and Drug Administration had asked for additional data and product changes before it would consider approving Calypte's HIV-1 confirmation test, which is a companion to its urine-based test for HIV-1.</p>
<p>&quot;Until we are able to bring the considerable benefits of a simple, non-invasive complete testing system for HIV-1 to the medical community...we have taken steps to reduce spending and conserve cash,&quot; said Jack Davis, chief executive officer.</p>
